{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01MgWUDh8H79uK9fTkUDGF2B","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntiers:\n  best:\n    meaning: \"DDR decoding-agnostic 升级被 reviewer 认可为核心贡献加固，writing 修复到位，Findings 稳进\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"Decoding-agnostic DDR (greedy mean |d|=0.05) 被接受为 DDR 是 autoregressive 内在属性的强证据，Claim 2 从 'empirical observation' 升级为 'structural property'\"\n      - \"Task formulation (depth classification beyond binary) 被认可为 novel 且有实际意义——reviewer 不质疑 'who needs this'\"\n      - \"Base-model-only scope 被视为 honest boundary 而非 fatal flaw，instruct 退化数据 (OLMo-Instruct 0.338 vs 0.763) 作为 scope 证据被接受\"\n      - \"Negative finding (Claim 3, TOST p=1.1e-4) 被视为 intellectual honesty 的加分项\"\n      - \"72h 内完成全部写作修复：related work 补齐、decoding-agnostic section 整合、limitation 措辞精确化\"\n    number_ranges:\n      avg_reviewer_overall: [3.5, 4.0]\n      avg_soundness: [3.5, 4.0]\n      findings_accept_prob: [0.75, 0.90]\n      writing_fix_completion: [0.90, 1.0]\n      effective_claim_strength_delta: [\"+0.3\", \"+0.5\"]  # decoding-agnostic 对 Claim 2 说服力提升（相对于无该实验的 baseline，reviewer 感知尺度）\n      reviewer_scope_concern_severity: [1, 2]  # 1-5 scale, 1=minor mention, 5=fatal\n    narrative_direction: \"Original framing 完全成立。DDR 作为 decoding-agnostic autoregressive property 是 headline，三条 claims 无需降级。Abstract 可写 'DDR is an intrinsic property of autoregressive generation, independent of decoding strategy'。Contribution positioning 从 'empirical characterization' 微升为 'empirical discovery of a structural regularity'。Negative finding 正面叙事：depth fingerprinting is diagnostic, not curative — a principled scope boundary.\"\n\n  median:\n    meaning: \"DDR decoding-agnostic 被承认但 reviewer 认为 scope 限制削弱了 generalizability claim，需 rebuttal 或小幅调整后 borderline accept\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"Decoding-agnostic DDR 被认可为有意义的 robustness check，但 reviewer 认为仅 greedy + top-k 两种策略不足以 claim 'decoding-agnostic'——要求补 nucleus sampling 或 beam search（无法在 72h 内做）\"\n      - \"至少一位 reviewer 质疑 base-model-only scope 的实际价值：'in practice people use instruct models, so what's the use case?'\"\n      - \"0.694 binary F1 被认为 'moderate'——不足以支撑 practical utility claim，但足以支撑 'proof of concept' 级别\"\n      - \"Claim 3 negative finding 被接受但 reviewer 认为实验设计有限（3 seeds, single perplexity metric），要求更多 downstream task\"\n      - \"72h 写作修复完成 70-85%：核心 section 到位但 related work 或 appendix 仍有粗糙处\"\n    number_ranges:\n      avg_reviewer_overall: [3.0, 3.5]\n      avg_soundness: [3.0, 3.5]\n      findings_accept_prob: [0.40, 0.65]\n      writing_fix_completion: [0.70, 0.85]\n      effective_claim_strength_delta: [\"+0.1\", \"+0.2\"]\n      reviewer_scope_concern_severity: [3, 4]\n    narrative_direction: \"Claim 2 措辞从 'decoding-agnostic property' 软化为 'robust across tested decoding strategies (greedy, top-k)'，留出 hedging 空间。Claim 1 的 0.694 F1 重新定位为 'first baseline for a novel task' 而非 'practical tool'。需在 rebuttal 中强调：(1) base model scope 是 intentional contribution boundary 而非 oversight，(2) instruct 退化本身是 finding，(3) 0.694 是 LOGO leak-free 的 conservative estimate。可能需要加一段 'Practical Implications' 明确说明 use case 是 training data auditing 而非 deployment-time detection。\"\n\n  worst:\n    meaning: \"Reviewer 认为 scope 太窄、F1 太低、task motivation 不足，Findings 被拒，需 reframe 后投 fallback venue\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"多位 reviewer 认为 base-model-only + temperature [0.5,0.9] 的 scope 在 2026 年几乎没有实际意义——instruct/chat models 主导生成内容\"\n      - \"0.694 binary F1 被认为不足以支撑任何 classification claim——reviewer 指出 random baseline 在 balanced binary 是 0.5，0.694 的 margin 太小\"\n      - \"Task formulation 本身被质疑：reviewer 认为 depth classification 是人造问题，real-world contamination 不遵循 clean chain 假设\"\n      - \"DDR decoding-agnostic 被视为 incremental robustness check 而非贡献升级\"\n      - \"Negative finding 被视为 'so the method has no practical use?'——加深了 motivation 质疑\"\n      - \"写作未充分修复，presentation 问题加剧了 reviewer 负面印象\"\n    number_ranges:\n      avg_reviewer_overall: [2.0, 3.0]\n      avg_soundness: [2.5, 3.0]\n      findings_accept_prob: [0.05, 0.25]\n      writing_fix_completion: [0.50, 0.70]\n      effective_claim_strength_delta: [\"+0.0\", \"+0.1\"]\n      reviewer_scope_concern_severity: [4, 5]\n    narrative_direction: \"核心 framing 失效，需要找新 angle 但不降级目标（仍投同级 venue ICLR 2027 或 NAACL 2027）。Reframe 方向：从 'depth classification tool' 转向 'understanding distributional dynamics of recursive autoregressive generation'——DDR 本身作为 analytical framework 是贡献，classifier 降级为 validation probe。Paper 重心从 Claim 1 (classification performance) 转移到 Claim 2 (DDR characterization) + decoding-agnostic 作为主线。Title 从 'depth fingerprinting' 转向 'differential depth response in autoregressive text generation'。Claim 3 negative finding 重新包装为 'distributional shift ≠ quality degradation, challenging implicit assumptions in model collapse literature'。这个 reframe 放弃 practical utility 叙事，转向 understanding/characterization 贡献，更适合 Findings 的 empirical contribution 定位。\"\n\nconsistency_check:\n  metric_monotonicity:\n    - \"findings_accept_prob: best [0.75,0.90] > median [0.40,0.65] > worst [0.05,0.25] ✓\"\n    - \"avg_reviewer_overall: best [3.5,4.0] > median [3.0,3.5] > worst [2.0,3.0] ✓\"\n    - \"writing_fix_completion: best [0.90,1.0] > median [0.70,0.85] > worst [0.50,0.70] ✓\"\n    - \"scope_concern_severity: best [1,2] < median [3,4] < worst [4,5] ✓ (lower=better)\"\n  experimental_metrics_fixed: \"所有实验指标（F1=0.694, DDR greedy |d|=0.05, TOST p=1.1e-4 等）跨三档不变——变化的是 reviewer 对同一组数字的解读和写作呈现的有效性\"\n  tier_transition_drivers:\n    best_to_median: \"Reviewer 对 'decoding-agnostic' claim 的接受度和 base-model scope 的容忍度\"\n    median_to_worst: \"Task motivation 是否成立 + F1 水平是否被视为 meaningful\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":24590,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":24590},"output_tokens":19,"